    "recommendations": "• Trim vegetation along the driveway and walkway edges so responders can move quickly between the street, main residence, and detached structure without obstruction.\n• Cut back dense vegetation growing close to the main residence and detached structure so responders can reach all sides of both buildings.\n• Clear a walking path between the main residence and detached structure wide enough for two people to pass with equipment.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective markers so responders can identify the primary access point quickly at night or in low-visibility conditions.\n• Post address numbers at the street that are large enough to read from a moving vehicle.\n• Thin dense vegetation that blocks sightlines between the street and the main residence so responders can see the structure on approach.\n• Identify which access points lead to the detached structure and mark them clearly so responders do not lose time searching.\n• Keep vehicle parking areas clear of stored items so responders have room to stage equipment close to the structures.\n• Trim vegetation overhanging the walkway so responders carrying equipment can move through without obstruction."
